Package: elquantile
Type: Package
Title: Empirical Likelihood Quantile Inference and Study Planning
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Janis", "Gredzens", role = "cre", email = "janis.gredzens@lu.lv", comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0009-4890-4897"))
    )
Description: Empirical likelihood inference for population quantiles.
    Implements unsmoothed empirical likelihood, Adimari interpolation,
    Chen-Hall smoothing and Bartlett corrections, Zhou-Jing kernel substitution,
    and pseudo-observation adjusted empirical likelihood. Supports one sample,
    paired differences, independent quantile differences, independent group
    comparisons, and multiplicity-adjusted post-hoc tests. Includes local
    asymptotic, exact count-based, and Monte Carlo power calculations and
    sample-size planning. Multi-group extensions use first-order calibration;
    one-sample higher-order results are not asserted for these extensions.
Maintainer: Janis Gredzens <janis.gredzens@lu.lv>
